---
title: 'Removed Executors'
description: 'Nx 24 removes 35 deprecated executors across 14 plugins in favor of inferred targets. Learn which executors were removed and how the automatic migration converts your workspace.'
sidebar:
  hidden: true
weight: .1
filter: 'type:References'
---

Nx 24 removes 35 executors that were deprecated in Nx 23. Each removed executor has an inferred equivalent provided by its plugin, so the task you ran before still runs after the migration, just without an executor entry in your project configuration.

Installing Nx 24 does not break a workspace that still references these executors. The project graph still loads, and `nx migrate` still runs. Tasks that use a removed executor fail until you complete the migration.

## Removed executors

| Plugin             | Removed executors                                                                                   |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `@nx/cypress`      | `cypress`                                                                                           |
| `@nx/detox`        | `build`, `test`                                                                                     |
| `@nx/eslint`       | `lint`                                                                                              |
| `@nx/expo`         | `build`, `export`, `install`, `prebuild`, `run`, `serve`, `start`, `submit`                         |
| `@nx/jest`         | `jest`                                                                                              |
| `@nx/next`         | `build`, `server`                                                                                   |
| `@nx/playwright`   | `playwright`                                                                                        |
| `@nx/react-native` | `build-android`, `build-ios`, `bundle`, `pod-install`, `run-android`, `run-ios`, `start`, `upgrade` |
| `@nx/rollup`       | `rollup`                                                                                            |
| `@nx/rspack`       | `rspack`, `dev-server`                                                                              |
| `@nx/storybook`    | `storybook`, `build`                                                                                |
| `@nx/vite`         | `build`, `dev-server`, `preview-server`                                                             |
| `@nx/vitest`       | `test`                                                                                              |
| `@nx/webpack`      | `webpack`, `dev-server`                                                                             |

The old `@nrwl`-scoped aliases of these executors are removed as well.

Executors that have no inferred equivalent stay: `@nx/expo:build-list`, `@nx/expo:sync-deps`, `@nx/expo:update`, `@nx/expo:ensure-symlink`, `@nx/react-native:storybook`, `@nx/react-native:sync-deps`, `@nx/react-native:ensure-symlink`, `@nx/webpack:ssr-dev-server`, `@nx/rspack:ssr-dev-server`, `@nx/playwright:merge-reports`, and `@nx/playwright:wait-for-webserver`.

## Removed programmatic exports

Code that imported an executor function directly needs to call the tool instead.

| Package                | Removed exports                                                           |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `@nx/playwright`       | `playwrightExecutor`                                                      |
| `@nx/rollup`           | `rollupExecutor`, `createRollupOptions`                                   |
| `@nx/vite/executors`   | `viteBuildExecutor`, `viteDevServerExecutor`, `vitePreviewServerExecutor` |
| `@nx/vitest/executors` | `vitestExecutor`                                                          |
| `@nx/webpack`          | `webpackExecutor`, `WebpackExecutorEvent`                                 |

The executor option types, such as `ViteBuildExecutorOptions` and `PlaywrightExecutorSchema`, are still exported.

## Changed generator APIs

Generators no longer accept the `addPlugin` option. They always add their inference plugin, so remove `addPlugin` from code that calls them.

The `@nx/react:setup-ssr` generator is removed. It configured server builds on the removed `@nx/webpack:webpack` and `@nx/rspack:rspack` executors.

`getViteE2EWebServerInfo` and `getReactRouterE2EWebServerInfo` from `@nx/vite`, `getWebpackE2EWebServerInfo` from `@nx/webpack`, `getRspackE2EWebServerInfo` from `@nx/rspack` and `getRsbuildE2EWebServerInfo` from `@nx/rsbuild/config-utils` no longer take the `isPluginBeingAdded` argument. The port override moves up to the fourth argument, and the Vite helpers take the CI port override fifth:

```ts
// Before
await getViteE2EWebServerInfo(tree, 'my-app', configFilePath, true, 4200);
// After
await getViteE2EWebServerInfo(tree, 'my-app', configFilePath, 4200);
```

## Migrate

Run the standard migration. Each affected plugin ships a `remove-deprecated-executors` migration that converts your projects.

```shell
nx migrate latest
nx migrate --run-migrations
```

The migration runs `convert-to-inferred` for every project that uses a removed executor. It moves each target's options into the tool's own configuration file, registers the plugin in `nx.json`, and preserves your target names and configurations.

Some options have no equivalent outside the executor. The migration reports those rather than dropping them silently, so read its output before committing.

## Migrate a single plugin

To convert one plugin ahead of the upgrade, run its generator directly:

```shell
nx g @nx/vite:convert-to-inferred
```

Pass `--project` to convert a single project instead of the whole workspace.

## After migrating

Verify that the project graph still loads and that your tasks still run:

```shell
nx show projects
nx run-many -t build test lint
```

For the details of what `convert-to-inferred` changes and the options it cannot migrate, see [Convert to inferred](/docs/kb/convert-to-inferred) and [Troubleshoot convert-to-inferred](/docs/kb/troubleshoot-convert-to-inferred).
